1. Public IP Address
What is a Public IP?

A Public IP allows Azure resources to communicate with the internet.

Examples:

Virtual Machine
Application Gateway
Azure Firewall
Azure Load Balancer
Without Public IP
Internet
    │
    ✖
VM

Internet cannot reach the VM.

With Public IP
Internet
    │
    ▼
Public IP
    │
    ▼
VM

The VM is reachable (assuming NSGs allow the traffic).

Types of Public IP
Type	Description
Static	IP address remains the same
Dynamic	IP address may change when the resource is recreated or deallocated
Interview Tip

For production services, Static Public IPs are typically preferred to avoid changing DNS records.

Hands-on Lab 1: Create a Public IP

Portal:

Create a Public IP:

Name: pip-web-dev
SKU: Standard
Assignment: Static

CLI:

az network public-ip create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --name pip-web-dev \
  --sku Standard \
  --allocation-method Static

Verify:

az network public-ip list --output table
