Hands-on Lab 2: Create NAT Gateway

Prerequisites:

Public IP
NAT Gateway

CLI:

az network nat gateway create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --name nat-dev \
  --public-ip-addresses pip-web-dev

Associate it with your subnet:

az network vnet subnet update \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --vnet-name vnet-az400-dev \
  --name web-subnet \
  --nat-gateway nat-dev
3. Azure Load Balancer
What is a Load Balancer?

A Load Balancer distributes traffic across multiple backend servers.

Without it:

Internet
 │
 ▼
Server 1

If Server 1 fails, the application becomes unavailable.

With Load Balancer
Internet
    │
    ▼
Load Balancer
    │
 ┌──┴──┐
 ▼     ▼
VM1   VM2

Traffic is distributed based on the configured load-balancing rules.

Types
Type	Use Case
Public Load Balancer	Internet-facing applications
Internal Load Balancer	Private/internal applications
Layer

Azure Load Balancer works at Layer 4 (TCP/UDP).

It does not inspect HTTP requests.

