5. Azure Firewall
What is Azure Firewall?

Azure Firewall is a managed, stateful network security service.

Unlike an NSG, it can inspect and control traffic centrally across multiple VNets.

Example
Internet
      │
      ▼
Azure Firewall
      │
      ▼
Virtual Network
Features
Network Rules
Application Rules
FQDN Filtering
Threat Intelligence
Logging
DNAT/SNAT
High Availability
NSG vs Azure Firewall
NSG	Azure Firewall
Subnet/NIC level	Network-wide
Layer 3 & 4	Layer 3–7 capabilities
Simple traffic filtering	Advanced centralized filtering
No FQDN filtering	Supports FQDN filtering
No threat intelligence	Threat intelligence support
